drm/rockchip/ebc: release everything a failed probe acquired; free the custom LUT on remove

hrdl's direct-mode rework of rockchip_ebc_probe() acquires, in order:
two plain vmalloc()s (packed_inner_outer_nextprev at 3 * num_pixels and
hints_ioctl at num_pixels -- ~10 MB together on the PineNote's 1872x1404
panel), streaming DMA mappings of the two phase buffers (plus zero_handle
in the LUT-walk mode), pm_runtime_enable(), the custom LUT
(rockchip_ebc_waveform_init() vzalloc()s lut_custom.luts,
num_temp_ranges * sizeof(struct drm_epd_lut_temp_v2) -- 228 kB for this
device's 14 temperature bins) and two parked kthreads. Only remove()
gave the vmallocs and the mappings back, and nothing anywhere freed the
LUT. Every failure return between the vmallocs and the thread creation
leaked what came before it: the three -ENOMEM returns, the two
mapping-error returns (which unmapped the earlier mappings but not the
vmallocs), eight devm_* lookups, the manual runtime-resume fallback, and
rockchip_ebc_waveform_init() itself -- the one that fails on every boot
of wilkbook's direct image, because custom_wf.bin does not exist until
the CLUT one-shot compiles it from the device's own waveform: the
initrd's raw-loaded driver probes first, fails there, and the one-shot
rebinds. The 2026-09-03 probe-unwind patch restored the drm_init()
unwind, which that boot-path failure never reaches. The two
thread-creation failures and the drm_init() failure also left the
parked temperature thread alive.

Glass, 2026-09-04 (wilkbook generation 14, doc/status.md): the rebind
still logs "rockchip-ebc fdec0000.ebc: Unbalanced pm_runtime_enable!"
at 8.2 s, after "Unable to load custom_wf.bin" at 2.8 s;
/proc/vmallocinfo holds two 1926-page packed_inner_outer_nextprev
entries where one is live and eight 642-page entries where seven are
accounted for -- the failed first probe's ~10 MB, once per boot. Five
unbind/bind cycles of fdec0000.ebc with the reader stopped raised
VmallocUsed by 212-276 kB per cycle: one 57-page lut_custom.luts entry
per successful probe, never freed.

Give the probe a label chain in reverse acquisition order -- stop the
refresh thread, stop the temperature thread, free the LUT, disable
runtime PM, unmap zero_handle if it was mapped, unmap the two phase
buffers, free the two vmallocs -- and route every failure to the label
that undoes exactly what it had acquired. A failed manual runtime
resume (runtime PM compiled out) disables runtime PM and skips the
suspend it never got to. remove() frees the LUT once the threads are
stopped and the CRTC is shut down, where the two vmallocs already go.
The success path is unchanged.

The 2026-09-03 third-party audit's item 2
(doc/reviews/2026-09-03-third-party-audit.md); wilkbook
doc/upstream-register.md item 23. Applies on top of
linux-pinenote-7.1-probe-unwind.patch and keeps its err_stop_kthread
label and goto. Unproven on glass as of 2026-09-04.

